# uMusic

uMusic is a private, self-hosted, context-aware music system. It stores an MP3
library, plays music in a web browser, learns from listening behavior, generates
playlists for activities and places, and later synchronizes those playlists to
an offline-first iPhone application.

## Product goals

- Store and manage MP3 files on a private server.
- Play the library from a responsive web application.
- Learn from plays, skips, completions, likes, dislikes, and replays.
- Generate mixes for cycling, running, gym, focus, relaxation, and other contexts.
- Associate preferences with user-created places/geofences without exposing raw
  location history unnecessarily.
- Import MP3 files directly and support private, replaceable import adapters.
- Synchronize prepared playlists to an iPhone for background/offline playback.
- Store media on either a local Docker volume or a Docker-mounted shared
  filesystem such as GFS/GlusterFS.
- Extend an exhausted offline queue from the server and cache upcoming tracks
  while connectivity is available.
- Leave room for spoken-word and podcast support after the music experience works.

