## Planned stack

- Python 3.13 and Django 5.x
- Django REST Framework
- PostgreSQL
- Redis and Celery
- Django templates plus HTMX for the first web application
- HTML5 audio with Media Session integration
- FFmpeg/ffprobe for validation and metadata inspection
- Docker Compose for self-hosting
- Pluggable filesystem storage; local Docker volumes are the default
- SwiftUI for the eventual iPhone client

Exact dependency versions should be pinned when Sprint 0 begins.

## Development quick start

Docker is the canonical Python 3.13 environment:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build
```

Then open `http://localhost:8000/health/ready/`. See
[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for local tooling and verification commands.

## Delivery order

The backend is the product foundation. The web player and learning pipeline are
built and exercised before iOS work begins so that the recommendation model has
real data and the mobile app can rely on a stable API.

## Content boundary

uMusic accepts MP3 files that the operator owns or is authorized to download and
store. Import mechanisms are isolated behind adapters and disabled by default.
The operator is responsible for complying with source-site terms and applicable
copyright law. The project will not implement DRM circumvention, credential
theft, or access-control bypasses.
